DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function eellff__ffiillll() allows an application to specify a fill value for the
     padding inserted between two sections of an ELF file to meet section
     alignment constraints.  By default the ELF library uses zero bytes for
     padding.

     The ELF library will only pad bytes if the ELF_F_LAYOUT flag is not set
     for the ELF file.

